Apple initially planned to equip the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> lineup and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> with 16GB of RAM, according to the leaker known as "<a href="https://weibo.com/5143897135/5351100254260033">Instant Digital</a>."<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2024/04/apple-silicon-feature-joeblue.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-945652" /><br/>
The brief Weibo post does not say when Apple considered that capacity. The &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max feature 12GB of RAM, as <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/09/iphone-18-pro-and-pro-max-ram/">confirmed through Xcode 27</a>, matching the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a> Pro models. The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; is also expected to have 12GB, but the Xcode data used to verify the Pro models did not yet include the foldable.<br/>
<br/>
Rumors had pointed to 12GB for the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; well before launch. In April 2025, supply chain analyst <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/ming-chi-kuo/">Ming-Chi Kuo</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/04/24/iphone-17-air-12gb-ram-rumor/">predicted</a> that the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18/">iPhone 18</a> lineup would have 12GB of RAM. Analyst Jeff Pu <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/01/16/foldable-iphone-a20-pro-chip-performance/">projected</a> the same capacity for the Pro models and Apple's first foldable iPhone in January. A <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/12/foldable-iphone-12gb-ram-supplied-samsung/">March report</a> from <em>The Bell</em> said Samsung would supply 12GB memory modules for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
The global memory shortage is the likely explanation for the apparent change. The March report described sharply rising prices for the 12GB modules, while <em>Bloomberg</em>'s <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/mark-gurman/">Mark Gurman</a> <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/08/foldable-iphone-history-and-price-revealed/">reported</a> that memory costs led Apple to discuss a higher starting price for the foldable. Kuo also <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/10/apple-cutting-2026-hardware-shipments/">said</a> DRAM shortages were forcing Apple to scale back its 2026 hardware shipment plans.<br/>
